    turnFlow: 'Each turn all players simultaneously choose one card and reveal them together. Cards are placed in ascending order onto one of four table rows: each card goes on the row whose end card is lower than the played card and closest in value (smallest difference). If a card is the 6th on a row, the player takes the five existing cards as penalty (Horns) and their card starts a new row. If the played card is lower than all row ends, the player chooses a row to take and their card starts that row. After 10 turns the round ends; players sum their Horn points. The game ends when someone reaches 66 or more points; the player with the fewest total points wins.',
